From: XR1710G Community <xr1710g-community@localhost>
Date: Fri, 21 Aug 2026 18:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] net: airoha: keep local bridge traffic out of PPE fallback

The Airoha L2-cache-miss fallback asks the Linux bridge for an egress
path before deciding whether an unbound packet may be committed to PPE.
That lookup is valid for forwarded traffic, but a bridge-local FDB entry
also carries a destination port. When the bridge and a direct GDM port
share a MAC address, the local entry can therefore look like a normal
forwarding path and bind traffic addressed to the router back to the
physical port.

Reject local FDB entries in the bridge forward-path helper. Add a
second, driver-local safety boundary that refuses bridge-master and
egress-device addresses as well as same-ingress hairpin paths. All
rejected cases fall back to the normal CPU path; ordinary routed/NAT and
bridge forwarding flows remain eligible for PPE.

The failure was independently reproduced on Gemtek XR1710G with a
direct 10G GDM port after hardware flow offload became active.

--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_ppe.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_ppe.c
@@ -1247,6 +1247,7 @@ airoha_ppe_foe_prepare_bridge_subflow(struct airoha_ppe *ppe,
 	struct ethhdr *eh = eth_hdr(skb);
 	struct airoha_flow_data data = {};
 	struct net_device *master, *egress;
+	u8 daddr[ETH_ALEN + 2] = {};
 	int err;
 
 	if (!is_valid_ether_addr(eh->h_source) ||
@@ -1254,6 +1255,7 @@ airoha_ppe_foe_prepare_bridge_subflow(struct airoha_ppe *ppe,
 		return false;
 
-	ether_addr_copy(data.eth.h_dest, eh->h_dest);
+	ether_addr_copy(daddr, eh->h_dest);
+	ether_addr_copy(data.eth.h_dest, daddr);
 	ether_addr_copy(data.eth.h_source, eh->h_source);
 
 	if (!skb->dev)
@@ -1269,8 +1271,16 @@ airoha_ppe_foe_prepare_bridge_subflow(struct airoha_ppe *ppe,
 	if (!master)
 		return false;
 
+	/* A local bridge address must stay on the CPU path. A bridge FDB
+	 * local entry can still carry a physical dst when ports share a MAC.
+	 */
+	if (is_etherdev_addr(master, daddr)) {
+		dev_put(master);
+		return false;
+	}
+
 	rcu_read_lock();
-	err = dev_fill_forward_path(master, eh->h_dest, &stack);
+	err = dev_fill_forward_path(master, daddr, &stack);
 	if (err || stack.num_paths < 2 ||
 	    stack.path[0].type != DEV_PATH_BRIDGE) {
 		rcu_read_unlock();
@@ -1282,8 +1292,12 @@ airoha_ppe_foe_prepare_bridge_subflow(struct airoha_ppe *ppe,
 	 * can be an AP netdev (resolved to WDMA by entry_prepare), a direct
 	 * GDM netdev, or a DSA user port.
 	 */
 	egress = (struct net_device *)stack.path[1].dev;
-	if (!egress) {
+	/* Never turn a local port address or same-port hairpin into a PPE
+	 * bridge binding. The software bridge remains the safe fallback.
+	 */
+	if (!egress || egress == skb->dev ||
+	    is_etherdev_addr(egress, daddr)) {
 		rcu_read_unlock();
 		dev_put(master);
 		return false;
 
--- a/net/bridge/br_device.c
+++ b/net/bridge/br_device.c
@@ -397,7 +397,7 @@ static int br_fill_forward_path(struct net_device_path_ctx *ctx,
 	br_vlan_fill_forward_path_pvid(br, ctx, path);
 
 	f = br_fdb_find_rcu(br, ctx->daddr, path->bridge.vlan_id);
-	if (!f)
+	if (!f || test_bit(BR_FDB_LOCAL, &f->flags))
 		return -1;
 
 	dst = READ_ONCE(f->dst);
